Description: Forward Ctrl+Alt+M to the remote session instead of minimizing locally
 On this kiosk there is no window manager chrome and the client always runs
 fullscreen (no /f toggle exposed to the user) -- "minimize the RDP client
 window" has no meaningful UI to minimize *to*. Worse, Ctrl+Alt+M is a real
 in-application shortcut on the remote side (e.g. Google Sheets' "insert
 comment"), and xf_keyboard_handle_special_keys() intercepts it completely:
 the keysym never reaches xf_keyboard_send_key(), so it never reaches the
 remote session at all.
 .
 /action-script was investigated as a non-source-patch alternative and found
 architecturally incapable of solving this (confirmed by reading
 run_action_script()/xf_keyboard_execute_action_script() in this same
 source): the script only gets a chance to *substitute a different local
 action* for a hotkey it explicitly registers at pre-connect init -- this
 switch statement runs unconditionally afterward regardless of what the
 script registered, and no action-script output value means "forward this
 to the remote instead." A source patch is the only way to change this
 behavior.
 .
 Removes the XK_m/XK_M case entirely, so Ctrl+Alt+M falls through to the
 same path every ordinary key takes (the function's final `return FALSE`),
 which is what causes xf_keyboard_key_press() to call xf_keyboard_send_key()
 and forward the real keydown/keyup pair to the remote session -- a true
 forward, not a locally-simulated keypress. Ctrl+Alt+C (toggle-control) and
 Ctrl+Alt+D (disconnect) are left untouched; only Ctrl+Alt+M was reported as
 a problem.
Author: Slime OS <dev@mulai.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-08-14
--- a/client/X11/xf_keyboard.c
+++ b/client/X11/xf_keyboard.c
@@ -1049,12 +1049,6 @@ BOOL xf_keyboard_handle_special_keys(xfContext* xfc, KeySym keysym)
 	{
 		switch (keysym)
 		{
-			case XK_m:
-			case XK_M:
-				WLog_INFO(TAG, "<ctrl>+<alt>+m pressed, minimizing RDP session...");
-				xf_sync_kbd_state(xfc);
-				xf_minimize(xfc);
-				return TRUE;
 			case XK_c:
 			case XK_C:
 				/* Ctrl-Alt-C: toggle control */
